{
  "dom_id": "step-q69925",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$\\frac{3xz}{4}÷\\frac{2z}{5}=$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{3xz}{4}÷\\frac{2z}{5},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3xz}{4}÷\\frac{2z}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{3xz}{4}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2z} & = \\\\ \\frac{15xz}{8z} & = \\\\ \\frac{15x\\cancel{z}}{8\\cancel{z}} & = \\\\ \\frac{15x}{8} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the final step, we canceled out a common factor of $z$ in the numerator and denominator.",
